---
// biome-ignore lint/correctness/noUnusedImports: used in the template below; Biome's Astro frontmatter analysis doesn't see markup usage.
import { CalendarHeart, CircleQuestionMark, Heart } from "@lucide/astro";
// biome-ignore lint/correctness/noUnusedImports: used in the template below; Biome's Astro frontmatter analysis doesn't see markup usage.
import Button from "@/components/Button.astro";
// biome-ignore lint/correctness/noUnusedImports: used in the template below; Biome's Astro frontmatter analysis doesn't see markup usage.
import Card from "@/components/Card.astro";
// biome-ignore lint/correctness/noUnusedImports: used in the template below; Biome's Astro frontmatter analysis doesn't see markup usage.
import Divider from "@/components/Divider.astro";
// biome-ignore lint/correctness/noUnusedImports: used in the template below; Biome's Astro frontmatter analysis doesn't see markup usage.
import Hero from "@/components/Hero.astro";
// biome-ignore lint/correctness/noUnusedImports: used in the template below; Biome's Astro frontmatter analysis doesn't see markup usage.
import HouseSectionIcon from "@/components/HouseSectionIcon.astro";
// biome-ignore lint/correctness/noUnusedImports: used in the template below; Biome's Astro frontmatter analysis doesn't see markup usage.
import Section from "@/components/Section.astro";
// biome-ignore lint/correctness/noUnusedImports: used in the template below; Biome's Astro frontmatter analysis doesn't see markup usage.
import SectionHeader from "@/components/SectionHeader.astro";
// biome-ignore lint/correctness/noUnusedImports: used in the template below; Biome's Astro frontmatter analysis doesn't see markup usage.
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Queen City Magic">
  <Hero />

  <Section width="wide">
    <div class="intro">
      <SectionHeader>
        <HouseSectionIcon slot="icon" />
        The magic explained&hellip;
      </SectionHeader>
      <p class="intro__aside">
        (to the best of our abilities&ndash;we are pleasantly surprised yearly ourselves)
      </p>
      <p class="intro__body">
        QCMM is a homegrown festival celebrating magic in all its forms, drawn from every
        fandom we can dream up. We love, accept and welcome kind humans from everywhere and
        every walk of life who come for fun, friends, a little mischief and the desire to
        believe in the extra-special parts of this world — from beloved books to things you
        have to squint and concentrate to believe in. We're an army of volunteers who work
        year-round to make sure that thousands of visitors to our town have the best hour or
        long weekend possible in our delightful, charming and downright magical historic
        downtown.
      </p>
    </div>

    <Divider />

    <Card>
      <CalendarHeart slot="icon" size={22} aria-hidden="true" />
      <h2 slot="title">Save the Date</h2>
      <p>
        Last year's crowd braved the rain and turned it into one of our best festivals yet —
        thank you to everyone who showed up and made the magic happen.
      </p>
      <p>
        Mark your calendars: Queen City Mischief &amp; Magic returns <strong
          >September 26&ndash;27, 2026</strong
        >, with more mischief, magic, mystery and mayhem than ever. We can't wait to see you
        there.
      </p>
      <Button slot="cta" href="/events">Plan Your Visit</Button>
    </Card>

    <Card>
      <Heart slot="icon" size={22} aria-hidden="true" />
      <h2 slot="title">You Belong Here</h2>
      <p>
        The people who work tirelessly on this festival for months do it as a hobby and a
        labor of love. We update as much as we can, but with a free festival and a million
        moving parts, it's hard to keep everyone abreast of everything. Just stay tuned, trust
        that there will be more to do than you'll have time for, and relax into it&ndash;whether
        you see everything or just one thing. All you have to do is show up and be wowed by a
        place and event that even those of us who live here and work on it can hardly believe
        exists. Staunton is magic! You'll only be sorry if you miss it.
      </p>
      <Button slot="cta" href="/donate">Help Us Make the Magic</Button>
    </Card>

    <Card>
      <CircleQuestionMark slot="icon" size={22} aria-hidden="true" />
      <h2 slot="title">Learn more</h2>
      <p>
        Facebook is the best place to check for updates as we get closer to the festival.
        We'll also post an FAQ and maps here on the site as details are finalized. Our
        historic downtown comes through every year&ndash;local shops, restaurants and
        non-profits pitch in with facilities, food and fun, from face painting to crafts,
        though we don't and can't allow outside vendors. We're grateful to our state tourism
        corporation for helping us welcome 20,000+ visitors to QCMM.
      </p>
      <Button slot="cta" href="/faq">Read the FAQ</Button>
    </Card>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.35rem, 3vw, 1.65rem);
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--color-surface-gold);
  }

  p {
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .intro {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1rem;
    max-width: 38rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .intro__aside {
    font-style: italic;
    opacity: 0.8;
  }

  .intro__body {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
  }
</style>
